# **The only entry in the player's collision table that gives health back**, and
# the second of the five transcribed a round ago to get an input.
#
# GLZJ is level 29 as it starts (`zamn_assets password`). The target is the
# type-$14 object at (451,964) -- collision id $27 ($80:CA30), whose jump-table
# entry is `$80:FACF`: three health, ceilinged at the same ten `$80:EB2F`
# refuses to spend a first-aid kit at.
#
# **The route has to hurt him on the way, and it does.** `heal_at_full` is the
# entry's own refusal path and it reads zero here, which is the report saying he
# arrived damaged; `heal_capped` reads zero too, which says three did not
# overshoot, so he was on six or less of ten. Both are named and untaken rather
# than quietly missing.
#
# Nobody contests this one. At frame 4360 the object's record is still at
# (451,964) with the player eight pixels away at (459,961) and nothing else
# inside the box; at 4370 it is gone. That is worth saying because level 45's
# `$80:FAA4` object was lost to a monster standing on it on three separate
# routes -- collision id $0004 takes objects too.
#
# `zamn_cosim verify -f 4420` checks 65,448 calls with nothing declined and no
# divergence. It also holds three victim sites nothing else reaches:
# `victim_event_4` (id $34), `victim_ignore`, and `victim_latched`.
#
# Route: east, south around the block, then a long staircase north-west through
# the level's middle. Thirty-one legs, all of them fitted.

